Interpretation
--------------
- Raw inter-node network RTT same-AZ on ENA is ~65 microseconds (p50),
  sub-150us worst case. Network is NOT a bottleneck for dispatch.
- libpq SELECT 1 is ~10 ms p50, dominated by per-connection backend
  fork + auth + teardown (fresh psql process each iteration), NOT the
  ~0.065 ms network hop. A pooled/persistent connection would cost
  ~network + query (sub-millisecond). Relevant only if SPIRE opens a
  fresh remote connection per fanout; if it pools, the 10 ms does not
  apply per query.
- One 145 ms libpq outlier (p99=max) — single cold connection, not
  representative.
